-- title:
--   Characteristic-ℓ divisor expansions generate k(̃ j,̃ j_N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \nmid N$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in the set of nonunits of $A$, and assume its residue field $k =$ `ResidueField ↥A` has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed. The assertion is an equality of intermediate fields of the Laurent series field `LaurentSeries k` over $k$: the field `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N`, obtained by adjoining to $k$ the set `divisorExpansionsC k N` of all series $q$-expanded along divisors, namely $\{\,\mathrm{qExpand}\,k\,d\,(\mathrm{jqModC}\,k) : d \mid N,\ d \neq 0\,\}$, coincides with `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, obtained by adjoining to $k$ just the two elements `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k N = qExpand k N (jqModC k)`. Here `jqModC k` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` with coefficients mapped into $k$, i.e. the reduction modulo the residue characteristic of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$\ell$ counterpart, for $\ell \nmid N$, of the classical fact that the field of modular functions of level-$N$ type generated by all $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$, is already generated by $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$. It is used in the construction of the fibre at $A$ of the Igusa scheme of level $N$, in particular by the statements identifying the residue-field base change of the chart algebra with the chart ring over $k$ and by the level-$N$ curve-model comparison over the residue field.
